{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1408026-does-a-master-of-spirit-need-mind-5-to-boost-a-spirit\u2019s-gnosis-rage-or-willpower","id":1408026,"title":"Does a Master of Spirit need Mind 5 to boost a spirit\u2019s Gnosis, Rage, or Willpower?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-13T14:27:59-07:00","id":1408026,"title":"Does a Master of Spirit need Mind 5 to boost a spirit\u2019s Gnosis, Rage, or Willpower?","content":"So a Master of Spirit can create fresh new spirit entities with Spirit 5 and Prime 2. But to create a mind to go with that spirit, they need to use Mind. Since a Spirit\u2019s mind is their Gnosis, Will, and even Rage, does that mean to give spirits these stats, or to boost the stats of preexisting spirits, you must first have mastery of the Sphere of Mind as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T14:38:22-07:00","id":1408028,"title":"","content":"&quot;Mindless&quot; spirits that simply exist and perform some basic instinctive actions still have ratings in Gnosis/Willpower/Rage. Mind is necessary to give them a high level of intellect, though the line of when that's necessary is kinda fuzzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T14:48:36-07:00","id":1408033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1408026-does-a-master-of-spirit-need-mind-5-to-boost-a-spirit\u2019s-gnosis-rage-or-willpower?p=1408028#post1408028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Mindless&amp;quot; spirits that simply exist and perform some basic instinctive actions still have ratings in Gnosis/Willpower/Rage. Mind is necessary to give them a high level of intellect, though the line of when that's necessary is kinda fuzzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their cognitive functions depend on Gnosis, and Willpower is still a part of their minds. It seems without Mind, you are just creating a drooling emanation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T16:18:26-07:00","id":1408064,"title":"","content":"Says you, also the dreamspeaker paradigm is entirely animist so all things have spirits you just have to wake them up if they are slumbering which you can do at dot 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T16:22:34-07:00","id":1408065,"title":"","content":"There's a difference between awakening an object's spirit and creating a spirit from nothing which was the OP's concern.<br /> <br /> The problem is that Mage is fuzzy about this. You generally don't need Mind to create, say, a box jelly. But jellies still have neural cells that process stimuli and dictate physical responses. When an animal's brain gets complicated enough that you need to include Mind isn't given a simple bright line to follow.<br /> <br /> Spirits are in the same situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T18:09:20-07:00","id":1408083,"title":"","content":"Indeed. I am trying to figure out the general mechanics of it is so that I know what you can do with Spirit 5, and also what it would take to craft a useful spirit guardian for a chantry. The thing is, a spirit\u2018s \u201cphysical\u201d self is also their conceptual self. You can\u2019t create a spirit of war without giving it Rage, and Rage, no matter how you look at it, is a thing of the mind. Even for spirits. There ARE spirits that don\u2019t need Rage, Gnosis, and Willpower, these are emanations. But it seems underwhelming if you need Mind 5 along with Spirit 5 just to create or boost a spirit. Though I suppose you could add charms to a spirit simply by adding Spirit 5 and a rote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T18:33:29-07:00","id":1408087,"title":"","content":"I certainly don't think you'd need Mind to boost a spirit. You don't need Life to boost mental Attributes with Mind even though your brain is technically part of this. Once the spirit exists, boosting it should just be Spirit unless you're expanding it beyond the nature of a spirit in some fashion.<br /> <br /> I would personally rule that Mind is necessary to create spirits of at least human equivalent intellect or spirits capable of multiple order thinking at least (that is, a spirit that can think beyond, &quot;this enforces my spiritual resonances, so I do it, that doesn't, so I don't.&quot;)... yes it gets expensive, but being able to create custom spirits to your personal needs is a very potent ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T18:22:31-07:00","id":1408298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1408026-does-a-master-of-spirit-need-mind-5-to-boost-a-spirit\u2019s-gnosis-rage-or-willpower?p=1408087#post1408087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would personally rule that Mind is necessary to create spirits of at least human equivalent intellect or spirits capable of multiple order thinking at least (that is, a spirit that can think beyond, &amp;quot;this enforces my spiritual resonances, so I do it, that doesn't, so I don't.&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />... yes it gets expensive, but being able to create custom spirits to your personal needs is a very potent ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good ruling. I think this is the most logical way to go, and really wish this had been inserted in How Do You Do That.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}